GPT output fields are named literal_translation/dubbing_line because with plain 'literal'/'dubbing' gpt-5-mini copied the Japanese source into 'literal'. Replies are keyed by segment id via a strict JSON schema (not newline-split) since the old splitlines()+zip silently misaligned every later line when the model merged or split one. Over-budget lines are shortened automatically because the model only approximates character counts (one line came back 61/60). Translators are imported lazily so each backend needs only its own credentials; Google/NLLB return the same text as raw and polished because plain MT can't adapt length. Budgets are chars/second per target language (en 14), a rough proxy for speech rate until #6 measures real TTS duration.
